## Bold and Colorful Short September Designs

Long nails have more room. Short nails have more nerve, because a saturated colour on a small tip reads as a deliberate choice rather than an accident of length.

Deep merlot, forest green, and burnt orange are the three shades doing the most work in <strong>short september nails</strong> this year, and all three land just as richly on a short nail as a long one, sometimes more so, since there's less surface for the colour to fade unevenly across. A full opaque coat in one of these shades, finished with a high-gloss top coat, is the fastest way to a short set that still feels like a statement. For a specific shade breakdown by skin tone and undertone, <a href='/blog/september/september-nail-colors'>september nail colors</a> covers that decision in depth.

Chrome finishes deserve a mention here too, since a metallic topper catches light differently at short length. There's less curve for the chrome to wrap around, which means the finish reads flatter and more mirror-like, closer to a true chrome effect than it often does on longer, more curved nails.

For anyone who wants colour with a bit more movement, a two-tone half-moon in a warm rust over a nude base gives the impression of more design without adding any actual complexity to apply.

