## Most Durable Shapes If Your Nails Break Easily

What's the most durable nail shape for short nails? Squoval and round both outperform almond and square. Squoval's rounded corners remove the weak points where square nails chip, and round removes corners almost entirely, making it the gentlest option of all for nails that are already prone to snapping.

Durability matters more for <strong>short september nails</strong> than for any longer set. Breakage-prone nails usually got short for a reason, and shape choice matters more here than polish choice ever will. A sharp square corner concentrates stress at two exact points, and that is where a crack starts and travels. Squoval spreads that same stress across a wider, rounded edge, which is the structural reason it holds up better under everyday friction like typing, opening jars, or pulling on gloves.

Filing technique compounds whichever shape gets chosen. Filing in one direction, rather than a back-and-forth sawing motion, keeps the nail's natural layers from separating at the tip, and that single habit change often does more for durability than the shape decision itself. According to nail experts, keeping the free edge short and consistently filed, regardless of the exact shape chosen, remains the single biggest factor in preventing further breakage.

For anyone whose nails break at the same one or two spots repeatedly, squoval is worth trying first. It gives slightly more definition than round while still avoiding the sharp corners doing the damage.

